## yunohost
The canonical way to install yunohost is installing yunohost on a [top domain](/core/maindomain).

|Do|Don't|
|---|---|
|yourdomain.tdl| yunohost.yourdomain.tdl|

if you installed yunohost on a subdomain :
- in webadmin, the yunohost portal settings will be still located to yourdomain.tdl
- the yunoohost login form will be still in yourdomain.tdl/yunohost/admin

## app migration to yunohost app
if you want to migrate from an app to a yunohost app :
- create a testing domain MyApp.test so you can try out before sending your app to production
- install the yunohost app and a database manager as phpmyadmin
- give yourself access to [sftp](/admin/tutorials/sftp_on_apps).
- import the database and rename columns
- LDAP 
